{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.ColorSpectralCubicGeometry","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorSpectralCubicGeometry","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorSpectralCubicGeometry.branchSextic_palindromic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorSpectralCubicGeometry.branchSextic_palindromic","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorSpectralCubicGeometry.lean#L69-L78","doc":"**Palindromic symmetry of the branch locus.** `D` is palindromic, i.e.\n`z⁶ · D(1/z) = D(z)`: the six ramification points are stable under `z ↦ 1/z`\n(coefficients `[16,24,35,50,35,24,16]` read the same both ways). The reciprocal\nsymmetry of the branch locus is a constraint any prolongation residue sum on the\n`S_c` must respect. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorSpectralCubicGeometry.color_cubic_discriminant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorSpectralCubicGeometry.color_cubic_discriminant","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorSpectralCubicGeometry.lean#L56-L67","doc":"**Discriminant of the color spectral cubic.** For\n`C_z(X) = X³ + bX² + cX + d` with `b = z+1`, `c = z²+z+1`, `d = z³+z²+z+1`, the\nmonic-cubic discriminant `b²c² − 4c³ − 4b³d + 18bcd − 27d²` equals the negative\nbranch-locus sextic `−branchSextic z` (cross-checked against `sympy.discriminant`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorSpectralCubicGeometry.branchSextic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorSpectralCubicGeometry.branchSextic","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorSpectralCubicGeometry.lean#L50-L54","doc":"The **branch-locus sextic** `D(z) := 16z⁶+24z⁵+35z⁴+50z³+35z²+24z+16`\n(`= −disc_X C_z`). Its six zeros are the ramification points of the color\nspectral curve — the bases of the exceptional divisors `S_c`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}